  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S. Martino, near Campochiaro. The distances provided on the <em>Peutinger Table</em> make this place 5 miles from <em>Bovianum</em> and 8 miles from <em>Saepinum</em>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A large fanum sacred to \u2018Herculis Rani\u2019? at Campochiaro, the name of which is then preserved in the station mentioned on the Peutinger Table. Scholars like Adriano La Regina support linking this fanum to a place mentioned by Livy, although see the discussion by Oakley.",
  "reprPoint": [
